2026-10-09T00:10:45.4439003Z -- v5.3.0 — defrost: duty is measured, the derate is physics
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4439232Z   ok   the inferred estimator reads a real defrost as a PERFECT interval
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4439423Z   ok   an over-1 ratio can no longer park the derate above 1.0
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4439597Z   ok   five defrosting minutes in thirty is a duty of 1/6
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4439734Z   ok   and the interval counts as observed
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4440007Z   ok   a quiet interval is duty zero AND observed — that is real evidence
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4440194Z   ok   an unreadable flag yields duty zero but NOT observed
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4440400Z   ok   a defrost spanning an interval boundary keeps its second half
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4440618Z   ok   a sample stamped before the last does not subtract from the on-time
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4440749Z   ok   zero duty is no derate at all
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4440907Z   ok   the derate is 1 - duty x the loss multiplier
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4441099Z   ok   more duty is always a deeper derate, never a shallower one
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4441305Z   ok   and it is bounded below, so a latched flag cannot zero the pump
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4441470Z   ok   a measured bucket derates from its counted duty
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4441703Z   ok   and a measurement is never averaged with an inference of the same thing
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4441853Z   ok   an untouched bucket still derates nothing
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4442186Z   ok   the summary says which estimator a bucket rests on, and how many defrosts were actually witnessed
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4442514Z   ok   a duty outside [0, 1] is refused, not folded into the bucket
2026-10-09T00:10:45.4442797Z   ok   the range guard rejects only OUTSIDE [0, 1] — 0 and 1 still fold
